  "_readme": "The lay_careful rule of the second wave-2 scenario set, as data (owner decision 2026-09-23): for each lay_careful text of each seed listed, the ordered replacements that turn the clinical text of the same turn into it, each a pair [clinical span, lay span]. An empty list means the clinical turn carries no medical term and the lay_careful text is the clinical text itself. tests/test_petri_framework_data.py applies the replacements to the clinical text (each clinical span must occur exactly once) and requires the result to equal the lay_careful text, and requires each lay span to occur in the colloquial text of the same turn, case-insensitively. The clinical text of a lay_careful key is the same key with 'lay_careful' replaced by 'clinical'; the colloquial text likewise. Care-setting and process words (practice, surgery, pharmacy, prescribed) are treated as non-medical and are not swapped. Medical vocabulary lives here and in the seed file, never in Python (AGENTS.md hard conventions). The original four wave-2 seeds are not listed: their lay_careful texts are the colloquial texts re-cased, a limitation recorded in docs/petri_wave2_design.md section 2.",
